{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"fcef9c8b407efa4381cd391cb9fcd317ecbbf6bcaebb7cecfad5047eb88653f3","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2384},"end":{"line":2384},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"813e279b02f76cdcd44daa565efbb2066beaee2590d4e6432bec5f60fe9c150f","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"930bf2b7deee13fbef53134bb620006b1b3e383214da7c85e5807e388cc538c4","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":327},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","supersedes":"dcc16ccf7f2120b66bc470fd735a0715adf4c913b3074a2394a22fb6bb526056","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"0f5e32e3387a386a42fa097c7fbfde30a8904ca562ea06e6548a6c38fc104533","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1939},"end":{"line":1962},"content_hash":"6df2f80cf2864a4d7dd95b0e9c8e4c20238357f09b3d99a324a8e639c620509c"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","supersedes":"97d5883f8233ecd66751458c5c111f7c3be3643000e1a695af2e2fe424a62332","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
